# Line endings.
#
# The repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which checks text
# files out with CRLF. That is harmless for Rust sources and docs, but fatal for
# the files Linux tooling executes or parses: a shell script checked out with
# CRLF fails at its own shebang ("/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or
# directory"), and these particular files are copied verbatim into the portable
# Linux tarball, so the breakage ships to users rather than staying local.
#
# Pin them to LF regardless of platform. See docs/known-issues.md (KI-54).
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.policy        text eol=lf
*.desktop       text eol=lf
